WEBVTT

00:00.550 --> 00:03.080
I think we should come up 
with some new menu items!

00:05.760 --> 00:10.020
Yeah, you say that every time 
the seasons change.

00:10.940 --> 00:13.700
That was what came to your mind 
with fall coming up?

00:14.320 --> 00:15.320
No!

00:15.660 --> 00:19.040
We do need to come up 
with a fall menu, of course,

00:16.160 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.190 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.220 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.250 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.280 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.310 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.340 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.370 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.400 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.430 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.460 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.490 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.520 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.550 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.580 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.610 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.640 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.670 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.700 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.730 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.760 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.790 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.820 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.850 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:16.880 --> 00:20.450
<b>Episode 12: "Two Encounters"</b>

00:19.040 --> 00:20.450
but that's not my point!

00:20.810 --> 00:24.710
We need something incredible 
that'll represent our café itself!

00:25.100 --> 00:28.210
Something that'll be all over 
TV and social media!

00:28.770 --> 00:32.420
I think that's the kind of thing 
a popular café needs!

00:33.040 --> 00:35.850
And who's going to come up with it?

00:35.850 --> 00:36.720
Huh?

00:36.720 --> 00:39.880
You're just gonna dump it 
on Shiragiku-san again, aren't you?

00:42.080 --> 00:45.480
If you had an idea like that, we'd have 
started using it ages ago, right?

00:45.900 --> 00:48.970
Isn't he dumb? Doesn't he have a dumb face?

00:48.970 --> 00:49.980
Shut up!

00:49.980 --> 00:53.240
Um... I wasn't actually thinking all that...

00:53.240 --> 00:54.730
I'll make something!

00:54.730 --> 00:55.880
Please don't.

00:55.880 --> 00:57.290
Aw!

00:57.290 --> 00:59.000
Honestly...

00:59.000 --> 01:00.120
Hayato.

01:01.100 --> 01:04.910
I think coming up with new 
menu items is a good idea.

01:05.240 --> 01:08.170
I kind of like...

01:08.480 --> 01:10.950
how serious you are about stuff like that.

01:14.360 --> 01:16.550
I-I like that, too.

01:16.550 --> 01:20.540
It makes me think about how reliable you are.

01:22.990 --> 01:26.240
This is just a dropping contest.

01:26.240 --> 01:28.730
No matter who wins, it's just a game.

01:29.590 --> 01:32.270
Oh, you guys are making 
fun of me, aren't you?

01:32.270 --> 01:34.240
I'm not falling for that again!

01:34.870 --> 01:37.130
We won't be able to do this for a while.

01:37.130 --> 01:41.120
Yeah. He's all distrustful of us now.

01:41.120 --> 01:43.840
What's going on, Akane-chan and Riho-san?

01:44.250 --> 01:48.440
I told Hayato that I like him.

01:50.710 --> 01:54.170
Anyway! We need new menu items!

01:54.170 --> 01:55.690
Okay!

01:56.090 --> 01:59.340
<b>Cake Flour</b>

01:56.090 --> 01:59.340
<b>Silkit
Wet Tissues</b>

01:56.760 --> 01:59.340
You're really fired up for this, 
huh, Hayato-kun?

01:59.920 --> 02:02.850
You really offered to help me 
think up new menu items!

02:02.850 --> 02:06.140
Well, I don't want to have Ouka 
on my case all the time.

02:06.980 --> 02:09.850
Besides, your college classes start soon.

02:09.850 --> 02:12.730
I can't keep relying on you for everything.

02:12.730 --> 02:14.590
No need to worry about that.

02:14.590 --> 02:16.810
I'll make food to keep on hand.

02:17.360 --> 02:20.740
That might work for now, 
but I can't make you do it forever.

02:21.040 --> 02:24.250
You'll be moving out of here 
eventually, after all.

02:29.370 --> 02:32.280
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?!

02:32.280 --> 02:34.750
Why do you have to say sad things like that?!

02:34.750 --> 02:38.010
We'll always be family, won't we?!

02:38.010 --> 02:42.260
I mean, that's nice to say, 
but you can't work part-time forever...

02:42.260 --> 02:44.390
But I can still stay here, can't I?!

02:46.080 --> 02:48.280
I don't know if that'll work.

02:48.280 --> 02:51.650
Your parents probably 
wouldn't be too happy with it.

02:53.400 --> 02:54.940
Fine, then!

02:54.940 --> 02:58.400
If you're going to be that mean, 
I won't teach you anything!

02:58.680 --> 03:01.740
You can come up with the 
new menu items yourself!

03:05.080 --> 03:08.000
S-Sorry! I shouldn't have said that!

03:08.000 --> 03:10.880
You can stay here as long as you want.

03:10.880 --> 03:12.080
Really?!

03:13.070 --> 03:16.500
"The coffee you make really is good."

03:17.080 --> 03:21.750
"I do hope I'll be able to take my time 
enjoying it while watching the stars someday."

03:22.260 --> 03:24.480
Uh... What was that?

03:24.480 --> 03:26.310
Lyrics for a new song?

03:26.310 --> 03:29.590
I confessed my feelings to my crush, 
and that was his response.

03:30.160 --> 03:31.020
What?!

03:31.560 --> 03:33.840
I didn't even know you had a crush!

03:33.840 --> 03:35.860
And what kind of response is that?!

03:35.860 --> 03:39.640
I think he meant it's not out of 
the question, but it's on hold for now.

03:39.640 --> 03:41.610
He's just toying with you!

03:42.370 --> 03:45.490
What do you think? It's a sweet potato tart.

03:45.490 --> 03:48.040
Well, it definitely feels like autumn,

03:48.040 --> 03:50.700
and the ingredients 
probably wouldn't cost much.

03:54.470 --> 03:56.420
Time really flies, doesn't it?

03:56.760 --> 03:59.300
I can't believe September starts tomorrow.

03:59.900 --> 04:01.360
What brought that on?

04:01.360 --> 04:03.050
Nothing, really.

04:03.390 --> 04:06.550
I just realized how quickly summer ended.

04:06.550 --> 04:08.410
Yeah, I guess so.

04:08.410 --> 04:11.060
That's just how busy it was.

04:11.060 --> 04:13.130
Just busy?

04:13.810 --> 04:17.190
Didn't something else happen, too?

04:17.810 --> 04:19.570
Something romantic, maybe?

04:25.760 --> 04:28.040
Wh-What about you?

04:28.040 --> 04:32.280
If you're asking me that, 
something must have happened with you.

04:34.600 --> 04:36.970
Grandma was right.

04:36.970 --> 04:39.860
You really are a terrible liar.

04:39.860 --> 04:40.940
Huh?

04:41.640 --> 04:44.520
I know, y'know.

04:44.520 --> 04:47.050
You know... what?

04:51.760 --> 04:54.170
I have someone I like, too.

04:54.640 --> 04:57.690
But even if it turns out 
the feeling's mutual,

04:57.690 --> 05:00.110
I could never go out with him.

05:00.440 --> 05:04.780
Because I know I'd only make him sad one day.

05:05.480 --> 05:06.520
But...

05:07.400 --> 05:12.220
I was the first one out of all of us 
to fall in love with you!

05:12.750 --> 05:16.570
I just want you to know that.

05:18.840 --> 05:22.620
Wh-Where did all that come from?

05:22.620 --> 05:24.630
Are you drunk again?

05:24.630 --> 05:27.400
I'm being serious!

05:28.360 --> 05:30.890
Oh... Sorry.

05:30.890 --> 05:34.770
But when you hit me with that so suddenly...

05:35.290 --> 05:36.520
It's fine.

05:36.920 --> 05:38.300
Shiragiku...

05:42.080 --> 05:45.540
As long as I have this smell!

05:43.640 --> 05:47.410
You <i>are</i> drunk! How, though?!

05:47.110 --> 05:48.410
<b>Alcohol Disinfecting Wipes</b>

05:49.160 --> 05:50.670
Those again?!

05:50.670 --> 05:53.660
You're not allowed to clean up anymore!

05:54.110 --> 05:55.580
Come on!

05:56.580 --> 06:00.200
Let's do it before the others get back!

06:00.200 --> 06:01.670
Do what?!

06:01.670 --> 06:03.820
How goes the new menu—

06:06.340 --> 06:09.340
I can't get enough!

06:06.820 --> 06:08.710
Cut it out!

06:09.680 --> 06:12.680
You know, if you get too carried away,

06:12.680 --> 06:15.220
even I'm gonna get sick of you.

06:15.780 --> 06:17.130
H-Hey!

06:17.130 --> 06:18.410
Jerk.

06:21.800 --> 06:23.360
Jeez...

06:23.360 --> 06:25.980
She can get drunk that way, too?

06:25.980 --> 06:27.510
Still...

06:27.960 --> 06:33.160
How much of that did she 
say while actually sober?

06:35.680 --> 06:39.310
Sorry to make you go shopping with me.

06:39.310 --> 06:42.250
Nah, it's for our new menu stuff.

06:42.250 --> 06:45.130
And Ouka and Akane are watching the café.

06:45.560 --> 06:47.690
There was something 
I wanted to ask you, anyway.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.590
You know, for the autumn sale...

06:52.280 --> 06:54.090
Hey, Hayato-kun!

06:54.090 --> 06:55.240
Hello.

06:55.240 --> 06:58.750
What's this? On a date 
with Shiragiku-chan today?

06:58.750 --> 07:01.400
W-W-We're just buying supplies!

07:01.760 --> 07:05.520
Oh, right. We're thinking 
about new menu items.

07:05.520 --> 07:08.090
Do you have any good ideas?

07:08.780 --> 07:14.160
You two served some surprising dishes 
at the Cherry Blossom Festival.

07:14.160 --> 07:16.240
Oh, that stuff?

07:16.240 --> 07:19.160
Your grandma taught us how to make those.

07:19.480 --> 07:20.620
She did?

07:20.620 --> 07:21.790
Yeah.

07:21.790 --> 07:24.040
She always said you don't need 
expensive ingredients.

07:24.400 --> 07:29.420
It just takes a simple idea 
to make unique, delicious dishes.

07:29.420 --> 07:34.180
Yeah, comments like that hit different 
from a three-star restaurant chef!

07:33.200 --> 07:34.180
Hey!

07:34.180 --> 07:37.900
Huh? What was that about 
a three-star restaurant?

07:37.900 --> 07:39.180
U-Um...

07:39.180 --> 07:44.410
Oh, nothing! I just meant 
she was at that level!

07:44.410 --> 07:48.570
For crying out loud! 
Would you stop being stupid?!

07:48.570 --> 07:50.570
Let's go, Hayato-kun!

07:50.570 --> 07:51.570
H-Hey!

07:52.050 --> 07:57.500
I-I think it'd be best to use locally 
produced ingredients for our new menu!

07:57.500 --> 08:00.260
We're a seaside café, after all...

08:03.160 --> 08:07.090
You know something about my grandma, don't you?

08:07.090 --> 08:11.720
Huh? Where'd that come from all of a sudden?

08:12.190 --> 08:13.970
Okay, let me rephrase that.

08:14.670 --> 08:19.020
What is it you do in 
Grandma's room every night?

08:25.570 --> 08:28.980
Hey, Dad, what does that say?

08:28.980 --> 08:31.020
It says "Familia."

08:31.020 --> 08:33.520
It's Spanish for "family."

08:34.110 --> 08:39.490
My teacher, a goddess of cooking, is here.

08:40.870 --> 08:42.700
Welcome.

08:43.870 --> 08:47.360
I finally found you, Kasukabe-san.

08:47.360 --> 08:49.340
Is that you, Ono-kun?

08:49.340 --> 08:53.470
Yes. You taught me so much 
at the restaurant in Spain.

08:53.970 --> 08:57.970
I'm actually starting up 
my own restaurant in Tokyo.

08:57.970 --> 09:00.140
I wanted to let you know.

09:00.140 --> 09:01.420
Oh, really?

09:01.420 --> 09:02.730
Hey, Dad!

09:03.810 --> 09:06.300
Something smells good!

09:06.300 --> 09:09.310
Yeah, it sure does. It must be a cake.

09:09.310 --> 09:12.800
Kasukabe-san, this is my daughter, Shiragiku.

09:12.800 --> 09:14.190
Hi!

09:14.190 --> 09:15.900
Ah, so you're...

09:18.110 --> 09:21.580
I really wanted to introduce her to you.

09:22.010 --> 09:24.920
So you're a father now, are you?

09:24.920 --> 09:27.340
Oh... Well, yeah...

09:27.340 --> 09:29.080
Hey, Grandma!

09:29.080 --> 09:31.360
I want some cake!

09:31.360 --> 09:33.590
C-Come now, Shiragiku!

09:33.590 --> 09:35.220
But...

09:35.780 --> 09:37.310
I'm sorry.

09:37.310 --> 09:40.720
I'll give you some after it's cooled a bit.

09:40.720 --> 09:42.910
It's a pumpkin cheesecake.

09:42.910 --> 09:45.480
Wow! Pumpkin cheesecake?!

09:45.480 --> 09:46.990
Sorry about this.

09:46.990 --> 09:51.690
Oh, it's fine. It's a new menu item, 
so I'd like some opinions.

09:52.110 --> 09:56.700
By the way, I looked at the menu 
you have posted outside.

09:57.000 --> 10:01.390
It's all light meals, 
just like an ordinary café.

10:01.390 --> 10:07.850
Couldn't a chef of your skill run a 
much more impressive restaurant?

10:09.490 --> 10:10.730
Grandma!

10:11.080 --> 10:12.840
I'm hungry! I'm hungry!

10:13.540 --> 10:15.260
I'm hungry!

10:15.260 --> 10:18.000
Now, stop that! Just be patient!

10:18.000 --> 10:20.470
I'll make pilaf for you later.

10:21.010 --> 10:22.440
Stupid old hag!

10:23.220 --> 10:27.530
Hayato! Honestly, what an 
unlovable child you are!

10:27.530 --> 10:28.790
Um...

10:29.480 --> 10:32.980
Was that child, by any chance...

10:33.400 --> 10:35.600
My grandson, Hayato.

10:35.600 --> 10:39.440
Though I don't know who he got 
that sharp tongue of his from...

10:39.440 --> 10:41.880
Oh, right. Shiragiku-chan...

10:42.940 --> 10:44.790
Hayato-kun?

10:45.740 --> 10:49.250
Your grandma gave us ice cream.

10:49.250 --> 10:51.500
Want to eat it together?

10:54.160 --> 10:57.010
Where did Hayato-kun go?

10:57.010 --> 10:58.680
Is he outside?

11:07.650 --> 11:09.080
You!

11:09.080 --> 11:10.890
What have you done?!

11:10.890 --> 11:12.960
I just bought these shoes!

11:12.960 --> 11:15.270
I-I'm sorry!

11:15.270 --> 11:17.690
You think apologizing will fix this?!

11:17.690 --> 11:19.780
Being a child won't excuse you!

11:19.780 --> 11:21.860
Do you know how much these cost?!

11:22.560 --> 11:23.780
Um...

11:23.780 --> 11:27.040
Say something! Aren't your parents around?!

11:27.040 --> 11:30.020
<i>What do I do? Someone, help me...</i>

11:34.170 --> 11:36.780
It's not safe to stand right there, y'know.

11:36.780 --> 11:38.550
I'm cleaning up out here.

11:40.180 --> 11:41.600
You little...

11:41.600 --> 11:43.430
I told you it wasn't safe.

11:43.430 --> 11:45.300
You're in my way! Get out of here!

11:46.340 --> 11:48.330
Stop that!

11:49.190 --> 11:50.830
You won't get away with this!

11:50.830 --> 11:52.060
What happened?

11:52.060 --> 11:54.880
I think the boy sprayed some water on him.

11:54.880 --> 11:57.940
And he's that angry? Talk about childish.

11:57.940 --> 11:59.800
Who is he, anyway?

11:59.800 --> 12:02.200
That's Fuwa-san, the former ambassador.

12:02.200 --> 12:04.180
Oh, him!

12:05.590 --> 12:06.910
This isn't over!

12:07.230 --> 12:08.500
Stupid.

12:08.500 --> 12:10.220
U-Um...

12:10.910 --> 12:13.240
Th-Thank you.

12:13.240 --> 12:14.790
I hate that guy.

12:14.790 --> 12:17.790
He's always being mean to Grandma.

12:20.980 --> 12:23.550
Did that happen?

12:23.550 --> 12:25.640
I don't remember it at all.

12:25.640 --> 12:28.050
Well, you were really little.

12:28.050 --> 12:29.980
Why didn't you bring it up before?

12:29.980 --> 12:32.640
That was nothing you couldn't have told me.

12:33.880 --> 12:38.940
Because if I did, 
you'd know Grandma was a chef.

12:38.940 --> 12:42.160
And why shouldn't I know that?

12:42.160 --> 12:46.820
It seems like everyone who knew her 
was keeping it from me.

12:47.150 --> 12:50.330
I... can't tell you that.

12:51.000 --> 12:53.120
Please let me work for you.

12:53.120 --> 12:55.210
I got my dad's permission.

12:55.210 --> 12:57.080
Shiragiku-chan...

12:57.080 --> 13:01.460
I want to be a chef someday, so...

13:01.770 --> 13:03.920
Since my dad respects you so much,

13:03.920 --> 13:06.260
I want to learn everything I can from you.

13:07.620 --> 13:10.180
I promised Grandma.

13:10.790 --> 13:12.100
You did?

13:14.920 --> 13:16.310
I see.

13:16.700 --> 13:21.320
I could teach you how to cook when I'm 
not working at the café, if that's all right.

13:21.320 --> 13:22.810
Really?!

13:22.810 --> 13:27.120
But I need you to promise me one thing.

13:27.930 --> 13:30.810
The reason I quit working as a chef...

13:31.320 --> 13:34.850
If you do happen to see Hayato in the future,

13:34.850 --> 13:37.290
can you keep it a secret from him?

13:37.960 --> 13:42.410
But you can tell me anything she didn't 
swear you to silence on, right?

13:43.760 --> 13:51.600
Have you been looking every night 
for photos of her cooking in Spain?

13:53.860 --> 13:57.730
I hid them so Hayato won't find them,

13:58.140 --> 14:01.300
but maybe I should just get rid of them.

14:03.730 --> 14:04.910
Yeah.

14:04.910 --> 14:06.040
I see.

14:06.620 --> 14:08.360
I sort of understand now.

14:08.360 --> 14:09.110
Huh?

14:10.070 --> 14:12.860
I bet Grandma quit working as a chef...

14:14.250 --> 14:15.670
because of me.

14:17.500 --> 14:20.750
Hey, guys, look! I had this printed out!

14:20.750 --> 14:22.650
That's so cool!

14:22.650 --> 14:24.500
Yeah! It's a great photo!

14:24.800 --> 14:27.420
Hey, let's put it up in the café!

14:27.420 --> 14:29.100
Good idea!

14:29.100 --> 14:30.880
Where should we put it?

14:30.880 --> 14:32.010
Right here!

14:32.380 --> 14:34.650
<i>She went to Spain at age 43.</i>

14:34.650 --> 14:38.170
<i>The restaurant in Spain where she 
worked as head chef for 15 years</i>

14:38.170 --> 14:39.870
<i>became a three-star establishment.</i>

14:40.520 --> 14:45.900
<i>She then planned to launch a restaurant 
called Anhelo as its owner and chef.</i>

14:46.300 --> 14:49.020
<i>Right before its completion, 
she canceled the construction contract</i>

14:49.020 --> 14:51.080
<i>and returned to Japan. And then...</i>

14:52.210 --> 14:55.160
<i>She took me in—my parents 
had died in a traffic accident—</i>

14:55.530 --> 14:57.610
<i>and she started this café.</i>

14:58.860 --> 15:03.380
If she'd wanted to, she could have opened 
a restaurant after coming back here.

15:04.510 --> 15:07.080
But I got in her way.

15:07.080 --> 15:08.920
That's not true!

15:08.920 --> 15:12.490
You didn't get in Grandma's way at all!

15:12.490 --> 15:13.680
Shiragiku?

15:14.140 --> 15:15.930
You didn't know any—

15:15.930 --> 15:17.060
But it's true, isn't it?

15:17.440 --> 15:20.600
A three-star restaurant chef 
could've found investors.

15:20.600 --> 15:24.890
But to make it a popular restaurant 
that would be profitable,

15:24.890 --> 15:28.440
she would've been told to open it 
in a prime location in Tokyo.

15:29.200 --> 15:33.260
If she'd done that, I would've been alone 
in this big house all the time.

15:34.090 --> 15:38.040
So let's say she went into debt 
to open a restaurant here.

15:38.480 --> 15:41.040
With her skills, it would've been a hit.

15:41.500 --> 15:43.920
But then even I would have figured out

15:44.420 --> 15:47.030
the reason why she came back to this town.

15:48.090 --> 15:52.680
The restaurant she wanted 
to open in Spain, "Anhelo,"

15:52.680 --> 15:55.510
was named with 
the Spanish word for "longing."

15:56.390 --> 15:59.210
I know very well what kind 
of person Grandma was.

15:59.870 --> 16:02.600
She wouldn't leave her grandchild alone,

16:02.600 --> 16:07.450
and she wouldn't let him find out 
that she'd given up her dream for him.

16:08.550 --> 16:10.880
Which means she chose to be 
an ordinary grandma,

16:10.880 --> 16:14.140
even if it meant she'd always 
be struggling financially.

16:15.160 --> 16:19.120
That's why she gave up 
on being a chef, right?

16:19.120 --> 16:20.330
Well...

16:22.440 --> 16:25.210
By the way, are you one of those types?

16:25.210 --> 16:28.460
The kind who'll only date someone 
you want to marry some day?

16:29.380 --> 16:31.460
Huh?! Where'd that come from?!

16:31.960 --> 16:35.970
Well, you said you couldn't date the guy 
even if the feeling was mutual.

16:36.330 --> 16:39.100
And that you'd make him sad one day.

16:39.620 --> 16:44.890
The only way I'd ever figure out that your
 father was my Grandma's student

16:44.890 --> 16:47.610
would be if we got married.

16:48.630 --> 16:51.360
I took Grandma's dream away from her.

16:54.310 --> 16:56.810
I did ask her once!

16:57.740 --> 17:00.790
If she regretted quitting work as a chef.

17:02.120 --> 17:05.750
What? No, not at all. Not for one moment.

17:06.030 --> 17:10.750
But my dad said that cooking 
was your reason for living...

17:11.070 --> 17:15.960
The ten years I spent here 
with Hayato made me so happy

17:15.960 --> 17:20.640
that none of that even 
mattered to me anymore.

17:21.160 --> 17:24.070
See that scribble over there?

17:24.830 --> 17:27.040
Hayato drew that.

17:27.040 --> 17:29.820
It's by the seat that's 
the most clearly visible to me.

17:30.270 --> 17:33.060
That was his favorite seat.

17:33.790 --> 17:36.120
I didn't need a lot of money.

17:36.120 --> 17:42.730
Just watching Hayato grow day by day 
was my greatest happiness.

17:42.730 --> 17:46.100
He's just so precious, I can't help it.

17:47.160 --> 17:52.050
If I have a reason for living right now,

17:52.440 --> 17:53.820
it's...

17:56.120 --> 18:00.950
It's you! You were your 
grandma's reason for living!

18:01.550 --> 18:03.540
Of course you weren't in her way!

18:04.170 --> 18:07.940
She... never told me that.

18:09.900 --> 18:13.610
You know very well what kind 
of person she was, don't you?

18:20.070 --> 18:25.160
How many more times will I be able 
to see these cherry blossoms with you?

18:25.610 --> 18:28.290
As many times as you want?

18:28.290 --> 18:31.300
I'm pretty sure you're gonna live forever.

18:32.520 --> 18:34.510
Well, yes.

18:34.510 --> 18:39.430
I can't die until I've had a chance to torment
 the wife you eventually bring home.

18:39.430 --> 18:40.930
Huh?!

18:40.930 --> 18:42.440
Don't do that!

18:49.320 --> 18:51.600
Yeah, you're right.

18:51.600 --> 18:55.720
I got a lifetime's worth of Grandma's 
love right here, in this café.

18:56.780 --> 19:00.070
That's why I can't let it go under.

19:01.990 --> 19:05.700
You know, when Grandma died, 
I made a decision.

19:06.010 --> 19:07.100
Oh?

19:07.100 --> 19:12.500
If you ever came back here and said 
you would take over the café,

19:13.090 --> 19:18.070
I would support you 
with all I had, no matter what.

19:19.860 --> 19:22.920
To support you as your familia.

19:26.270 --> 19:27.380
I see.

19:29.240 --> 19:32.570
Well, then... I guess... 
I'll be counting on you.

19:32.570 --> 19:33.450
Sure.

19:36.370 --> 19:38.970
I'll work really hard, too!

19:38.080 --> 19:40.510
Me, too!

19:39.630 --> 19:41.990
Grandma!

19:41.080 --> 19:42.560
Hey, guys...

19:44.740 --> 19:48.120
You guys were eavesdropping again?

19:48.410 --> 19:50.110
I bawled my eyes out!

19:50.110 --> 19:53.540
That's the most beautiful 
story I've heard all year!

19:54.220 --> 19:55.300
You guys...

19:56.880 --> 19:59.050
I hate you, Hayato-kun!

19:59.050 --> 20:00.630
But... Grandma!

20:01.090 --> 20:03.850
I love her!

20:02.870 --> 20:06.390
Oh, shut up, all of you!

20:08.660 --> 20:11.930
Hi! I'm home!

20:15.140 --> 20:16.440
What's this?

20:16.440 --> 20:17.920
Sheesh.

20:17.920 --> 20:20.070
It's too hot for all that yelling.

20:21.120 --> 20:22.570
I'm home, Daddy!

20:22.570 --> 20:24.280
Don't call me "Daddy."

20:24.280 --> 20:27.490
Call me "Dad" or "Hayato-sensei."

20:27.490 --> 20:31.620
Why do I have to call my own dad "Sensei"?

20:31.620 --> 20:36.060
Who do you think got you through 
middle school without a failing grade?

20:38.360 --> 20:41.380
Hey, anyway, this is Mom 
in this picture, right?

20:41.380 --> 20:44.010
Yeah. I'm surprised you could tell.

20:44.010 --> 20:46.640
Well, she hasn't changed that much!

20:46.640 --> 20:48.640
Wow, she's so young here!

20:49.090 --> 20:51.980
Wait, are these other four women...

20:51.980 --> 20:55.350
I just came across it 
when I was cleaning the room.

20:55.350 --> 20:57.480
I'm putting it away.

20:58.690 --> 21:00.240
Hey!

21:00.240 --> 21:03.440
It's such a nice picture! 
We should put it up!

21:04.480 --> 21:05.450
Hey...

21:05.450 --> 21:09.280
Mom was still just working here part-time 
when this was taken, right?

21:09.280 --> 21:10.090
Yeah.

21:10.590 --> 21:13.710
So when did you fall in love with her?

21:15.800 --> 21:16.960
Who knows?

21:16.960 --> 21:19.550
It was too long ago. I forgot.

21:19.550 --> 21:21.320
Aw!

21:23.570 --> 21:25.500
Wow!

21:25.500 --> 21:27.470
You can see so far!

21:27.470 --> 21:28.970
I know!

21:28.970 --> 21:31.350
Indeed! But the waves are high!

21:31.350 --> 21:34.730
Why do we have to have 
a picnic on our day off?

21:34.730 --> 21:38.040
Hayacchi! I'm hungry!

21:38.040 --> 21:40.400
Come on, Hayato-kun! Lay out the sheet!

21:40.400 --> 21:41.480
Yeah, yeah.

21:41.480 --> 21:44.110
It looks so good!

21:44.110 --> 21:46.440
Let's eat!

21:47.680 --> 21:49.800
Yum!

21:49.800 --> 21:51.390
By the way, Shiragiku-san...

21:51.390 --> 21:52.240
What?

21:52.240 --> 21:54.700
What were you guys talking about?

21:54.700 --> 21:57.370
I heard something about 
marrying whoever you date,

21:57.370 --> 22:00.130
and not being able to date someone, 
even if the feeling's mutual.

22:00.130 --> 22:03.760
Oh... That was my, uh...

22:03.760 --> 22:06.260
Wh-What's going on, Kiku-chan?

22:06.260 --> 22:08.030
Oh, that's right!

22:08.030 --> 22:11.640
I don't have to keep 
Grandma's past secret anymore...

22:12.140 --> 22:15.430
So I can be a candidate for 
Hayato-kun's girlfriend, too!

22:17.560 --> 22:21.020
And if I end up marrying him someday...

22:21.390 --> 22:23.030
A candidate for his girlfriend?

22:23.460 --> 22:26.530
Wait, Shiragiku-san, 
are you saying you're in...

22:27.600 --> 22:31.530
And you said "too"! 
Does that mean there are others

22:31.530 --> 22:33.620
who like Hayato-kun?!

22:34.790 --> 22:37.410
U-Uh, no, that's not what I meant!

22:37.410 --> 22:39.450
I don't have any kind of...

22:40.980 --> 22:43.510
Kiku-chan! That's my cup!

22:44.670 --> 22:46.680
It's wine!

22:46.680 --> 22:48.390
What?!

22:49.120 --> 22:50.550
Meow!

22:50.890 --> 22:52.930
Meow, meow, meow!

22:53.240 --> 22:57.310
That's right! I love Hayato-kun!

22:57.310 --> 22:58.680
Stop it!

22:58.680 --> 23:00.400
Well, this isn't good.

23:00.400 --> 23:02.690
How long has she been drunk, I wonder...

23:03.150 --> 23:05.680
We're in public view here! We gotta stop her!

23:06.110 --> 23:09.990
When we're done making food, 
why don't we make a baby?

23:09.990 --> 23:11.070
Are you nuts?!

23:13.040 --> 23:14.750
No way!

23:14.750 --> 23:17.530
Stop it!

23:17.530 --> 23:20.000
<i>It's said that there are goddesses</i>

23:20.000 --> 23:22.330
<i>living in an old coffee shop 
on a beach somewhere.</i>

23:23.230 --> 23:27.630
<i>Will these five be the goddesses 
of good fortune who save this café,</i>

23:27.630 --> 23:30.300
<i>or the devils of poverty that sink it?</i>

23:30.970 --> 23:32.700
Come on in!

23:32.700 --> 23:35.810
Welcome to Café Terrace Familia!

23:36.120 --> 23:40.820
<i>Either way, I've gotten tangled up 
with some real pains in the rear.</i>
